From: MastaG <mastag@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: enable the VCN 2.0 video block on the BC-250

Cyan Skillfish reports UVD/VCN 2.0.3 in its IP discovery table, but
mainline skips the block, so there is no hardware video decode or encode.
Add vcn_v2_0 for the BC-250 (PCI device 0x13fe), behind amdgpu.bc250_vcn=1
(default off: a failed bring-up hangs the board at boot, seen on the test
board), with the bring-up changes
the ps5-linux project found for this silicon (ps5-linux-patches PR #38,
which does the same for the PS5, device 0x13fb):

- one VCN instance, rings without doorbells
- firmware amdgpu/ps5_vcn.bin instead of the IP-version name; it is not in
  linux-firmware and comes from the bc250-vcn-fw package. Without the file
  the VCN block is simply left out and the rest of amdgpu is unaffected.
- power gating is left off at start, the block is soft reset in a fixed
  order, and a firmware that never reports ready returns -ETIMEDOUT
- stop falls back to a reset when the block never goes idle
- the VCN firmware is never handed to the PSP: the BIOS-booted PSP of this
  board refuses ps5_vcn.bin (LOAD_IP_FW answers 0xFFFF0008, seen on the test
  board), as it is not signed for it, so the driver copies the firmware into
  the VCN buffer itself (the direct path the PS5 uses) while graphics and
  SDMA stay on the PSP
- "bc250-vcn:" messages mark each bring-up step and name each IP block whose
  hw_init is about to run, so the last one printed shows where a hang is
  (each waits 150 ms so the network console can send it before the next
  access)

No other board is affected: every change is keyed on device 0x13fe.

